    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5f080278419832dcf3d759c3165f03806711c455c4b09656143908b809a94433",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source reverses the conventional Goldbach search layout. Instead of sieving every high target interval and translating it by small primes, it precomputes the reusable small-difference prime set P, generates only a bounded list of primes q_i near each interval, and covers all targets by accumulating P+q_i. The set translations become shifted bit arrays whose OR records existential coverage, while bounded-base strong-pseudoprime results certify the generated q_i in the stated range.",
