    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_87939265fb034ac2038389022784aee22e783140941eccbe527ac735d479f17d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Assuming GRH, the source divides the three-primes result by numerical scale. Above 10^20 it seeks positivity of J(N) through a circle-method leading-term/remainder split; at or below 10^20 it subtracts a nearby prime so that the even residual is at most 1.615×10^12 and therefore lies inside the cited two-prime coverage through 10^13. The reported bitset computation supplies the upper portion of that finite coverage.",
